\section{Temporal-Symmetry-Preserving Computation}

TSSE requires that computation preserve temporal symmetry:
\[
\mathcal{T}\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}} = \mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}}\mathcal{T}.
\]

\begin{definition}[Temporal-Symmetry-Preserving Execution]
Kernel execution is temporal-symmetry-preserving if:
\[
\mathcal{T}\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}}(\mathcal{K}_i)
=
\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}}(\mathcal{T}\mathcal{K}_i).
\]
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Temporal Execution Consistency]
If $[\mathcal{T},\mathcal{K}_i] = 0$ for all kernels, then:
\[
[\mathcal{T},\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}}] = 0.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Commutation is preserved under deterministic ordering and kernel composition.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[Global Temporal-Symmetry-Preserving Computation]
The TSSE computational layer preserves temporal symmetry across all kernel executions.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Follows from kernel admissibility and the TSSE temporal operator axioms.
\end{proof}

This theorem ensures that TSSE computation respects temporal invariants.

