\section{Canonical TSSE Computational Kernel (TSSE-CKX)}

Define the TSSE Computational Kernel:
\[
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-CKX}} =
\left(
\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}},\;
\Phi_{\Delta t},\;
\Sigma_{\text{TSSE}},\;
H_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}},\;
\mathcal{T},\;
\mathcal{U}(t)
\right).
\]

It enforces:
\[
\mathcal{T}\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}} = \mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}}\mathcal{T},
\qquad
\Phi_{\Delta t}^\top J\,\Phi_{\Delta t} = J,
\qquad
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}} = \mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}.
\]

This kernel defines the complete computational execution architecture of TSSE engines.

